{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1484762-homebrew-supernal-invention-system","id":1484762,"title":"[Homebrew] Supernal Invention System.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-23T02:11:39-07:00","id":1484762,"title":"[Homebrew] Supernal Invention System.","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18bzOpIF9wIL9qRnef6jzXSD5E7BMF-YgDAyI8IMLUwU/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Click here to see it.</b></a> Feedback is very welcome. I co-authored this with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11880_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11880\" data-vbnamecard=\"11880\">Dark Archon</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-25-2022, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T14:59:56-07:00","id":1484808,"title":"","content":"I like this idea a lot, it gives mages more options for creating magical items. Its far less convenient that an imbued item, but with an improved accessibility level for non-mages. It has more complicated steps for creating them, yet is accessible to all Paths and tempting enough to ensure many would consider the investment. Its also a very nice system for creating Mysteries that crafting focused mages, especially those in a crafting centric Legacies, could pursue. Looking at the document itself, a few thoughts come to mind:<br /> <br /> * In the <i>Designing a Wonder</i> chapter, there is a lot information being delivered at once, for which readers do not have full context. I think it might be a good idea to start the chapter with something similar to page 67 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i>, a cheat sheet that allows for a top-down look at the systems and acts as a quick reference.<br /> <br /> * Since the system for creating Wonders could be seen as balancing a zero sum equation, then perhaps you could utilize the Blood Bathing ritual from <i>World of Darkness: Immortals</i> as a reference for the formatting. While it is what was implied by the writeup, I think utilizing such a format would make visualization easier.<br /> <br /> * The Operator Drawbacks are probably not always negatives. If a Wonder can only be used by Mysterium Egregores, then it means there is no point in stealing it, since it would take extra work to get a traitor to use them.<br /> <br /> * Environmental Hazards could probably be broken down into more details. I think each Drawback point could become 1 per Environmental Hazard level. Similarly, perhaps the area of effect and duration could also be tied to points. This might lead to a situation where clever mages incorporate the drawback into the system, like a Wonder with Control Electricity that causes thunderstorms it can harness, but I would say that is working as intended.<br /> <br /> Those are my initial thought, hope they help","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-23-2022, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T16:48:21-07:00","id":1484823,"title":"","content":"I really like the design and idea. But I really have problems grasping concepts, for example how Passive and Active wonders work: If I want to create a clone machine, I only need a Live 5 Mind 5 mage or I need another Weaving spell that increases Wonder Rating?<br /> <br /> In general I find three things I feel weird:<br /> <br /> First, the extended action to create the Wonder is [Mystery Key <b>x10]</b>? That sounds like a lot, in general, the Keys are equal to the Wonder Rating so even a simple Wonder of Rating 3 needs 30 sucess in a Extended Action that [for what I understand] have a limit of Attribute+Skill attempts. You would need someone with 5 Intelligence + 5 Science for example and even there if they fail one or two rolls the wonder is unable of being created. Maybe I'm missing something here, but from my perspective the success needed are excesive in-universe.<br /> <br /> Second, I really feel this have the same problem I have reading Ascension on this things... You can give me, like, a detailed example? I read the rules and I find i understand, but maybe I'm understanding wrong. And even them, explain with examples is always fun!<br /> <br /> Third, I don't understand how Scale interact with the Wonder. If I create a Cloning Machine, I need scale the number of clones the machine can create at all? It says &quot;before recharging&quot;, but if I don't put a Fuel, Parts or Mantenaince Drawback, it don't need to be &quot;recharged&quot; no?<br /> <br /> I'm really excited for how you expand on others splats using this! Occultist using Essence as fuel is somewhat one of the pillars of my next Chronicle and having rules to the players imitate them is always useful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","user":"altidiya","date":".  Added a third thing I feel weird 06-23-2022, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T17:15:22-07:00","id":1484826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>altidiya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1484762-homebrew-supernal-invention-system?p=1484823#post1484823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the design and idea. But I really have problems grasping concepts, for example how Passive and Active wonders work: If I want to create a clone machine, I only need a Live 5 Mind 5 mage or I need another Weaving spell that increases Wonder Rating?<br /> <br /> In general I find two things I feel weird:<br /> <br /> First, the extended action to create the Wonder is [Mystery Key <b>x10]</b>? That sounds like a lot, in general, the Keys are equal to the Wonder Rating so even a simple Wonder of Rating 3 needs 30 sucess in a Extended Action that [for what I understand] have a limit of Attribute+Skill attempts. You would need someone with 5 Intelligence + 5 Science for example and even there if they fail one or two rolls the wonder is unable of being created. Maybe I'm missing something here, but from my perspective the success needed are excesive in-universe.<br /> <br /> Second, I really feel this have the same problem I have reading Ascension on this things... You can give me, like, a detailed example? I read the rules and I find i understand, but maybe I'm understanding wrong. And even them, explain with examples is always fun!<br /> <br /> I'm really excited for how you expand on others splats using this! Occultist using Essence as fuel is somewhat one of the pillars of my next Chronicle and having rules to the players imitate them is always useful!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is a topic with many <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\">magical items designed to be used by mortals</a>. The effects are pretty nice, although they come with curses and, if you don't have a character with an alternative morality system to Integrity, they also risk breaking points. I can see them being very useful for mortals in general. It might be interesting to see how difficult they are to craft using the Wonders system.<br /> <br /> Some other alternatives can be found in Hunter, The Vigil: Witchfinders (for how mortal occultists can bind a Familiar) and the line developer for Werewolf also made a post about homebrew rules for occultists <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1231346-those-who-call-to-spirits-human-occultists\">harnessing the power of the Shadow</a>. Its not even remotely good for the occultist's safety or sanity, but it is an path to considerable power. Should they pick the Pack Rite of the Fetish, they should be able to make all sorts of useful items. If they are skilled in diplomacy, maybe they could even negotiate for some Talens or the ritual to become a Purified immortal. Never underestimate the capacity of an insane mortal to become a monster of their own making.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T17:30:12-07:00","id":1484827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1484762-homebrew-supernal-invention-system?p=1484826#post1484826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There is a topic with many <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\">magical items designed to be used by mortals</a>. The effects are pretty nice, although they come with curses and, if you don't have a character with an alternative morality system to Integrity, they also risk breaking points. I can see them being very useful for mortals in general. It might be interesting to see how difficult they are to craft using the Wonders system.<br /> <br /> Some other alternatives can be found in Hunter, The Vigil: Witchfinders (for how mortal occultists can bind a Familiar) and the line developer for Werewolf also made a post about homebrew rules for occultists <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1231346-those-who-call-to-spirits-human-occultists\">harnessing the power of the Shadow</a>. Its not even remotely good for the occultist's safety or sanity, but it is an path to considerable power. Should they pick the Pack Rite of the Fetish, they should be able to make all sorts of useful items. If they are skilled in diplomacy, maybe they could even negotiate for some Talens or the ritual to become a Purified immortal. Never underestimate the capacity of an insane mortal to become a monster of their own making.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really love how supportive are you!<br /> <br /> I still wanting see the approximation from this system because the Key mechanics sounds very interesting. Even in Genius the concept of Blueprint and Prototype aren't as present in the creation of genius wonders, and I feel is something that can add extra drama about inversors, testing, and even creative blocks as Keys.<br /> <br /> But I still will read this and the Exarch Cult you name the other day, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T18:10:25-07:00","id":1484830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1484762-homebrew-supernal-invention-system?p=1484808#post1484808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this idea a lot, it gives mages more options for creating magical items. Its far less convenient that an imbued item, but with an improved accessibility level for non-mages. It has more complicated steps for creating them, yet is accessible to all Paths and tempting enough to ensure many would consider the investment. Its also a very nice system for creating Mysteries that crafting focused mages, especially those in a crafting centric Legacies, could pursue. Looking at the document itself, a few thoughts come to mind:<br /> <br /> * In the <i>Designing a Wonder</i> chapter, there is a lot information being delivered at once, for which readers do not have full context. I think it might be a good idea to start the chapter with something similar to page 67 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i>, a cheat sheet that allows for a top-down look at the systems and acts as a quick reference.<br /> <br /> * Since the system for creating Wonders could be seen as balancing a zero sum equation, then perhaps you could utilize the Blood Bathing ritual from <i>World of Darkness: Immortals</i> as a reference for the formatting. While it is what was implied by the writeup, I think utilizing such a format would make visualization easier.<br /> <br /> * The Operator Drawbacks are probably not always negatives. If a Wonder can only be used by Mysterium Egregores, then it means there is no point in stealing it, since it would take extra work to get a traitor to use them.<br /> <br /> * Environmental Hazards could probably be broken down into more details. I think each Drawback point could become 1 per Environmental Hazard level. Similarly, perhaps the area of effect and duration could also be tied to points. This might lead to a situation where clever mages incorporate the drawback into the system, like a Wonder with Control Electricity that causes thunderstorms it can harness, but I would say that is working as intended.<br /> <br /> Those are my initial thought, hope they help</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks! Here are my responses for your observations:<br /> <br /> * I will check out that part of Signs Of Sorcery, and see what can be done about a more reader-friendly format.<br /> <br /> * Right, that makes sense. I might borrow layout ideas from Unchained Pacts, maybe.<br /> <br /> * That is correct. One of the main goals of the system is to give instructions on how to pull off Genius-style inventions (the name &quot;Wonders&quot; is even borrowed from Genius), but in a way that allows Sleepers to use them, however risky it may be. As a result, a Wonder which includes the Operator Drawback is by definition meant to be used by esoteric circles. If the inventor wants to broaden the types of possible users, he simply uses a different Drawback.<br /> <br /> * Fair point, I will try and think of some examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>altidiya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1484762-homebrew-supernal-invention-system?p=1484823#post1484823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the design and idea. But I really have problems grasping concepts, for example how Passive and Active wonders work: If I want to create a clone machine, I only need a Live 5 Mind 5 mage or I need another Weaving spell that increases Wonder Rating?<br /> <br /> In general I find three things I feel weird:<br /> <br /> First, the extended action to create the Wonder is [Mystery Key <b>x10]</b>? That sounds like a lot, in general, the Keys are equal to the Wonder Rating so even a simple Wonder of Rating 3 needs 30 sucess in a Extended Action that [for what I understand] have a limit of Attribute+Skill attempts. You would need someone with 5 Intelligence + 5 Science for example and even there if they fail one or two rolls the wonder is unable of being created. Maybe I'm missing something here, but from my perspective the success needed are excesive in-universe.<br /> <br /> Second, I really feel this have the same problem I have reading Ascension on this things... You can give me, like, a detailed example? I read the rules and I find i understand, but maybe I'm understanding wrong. And even them, explain with examples is always fun!<br /> <br /> Third, I don't understand how Scale interact with the Wonder. If I create a Cloning Machine, I need scale the number of clones the machine can create at all? It says &quot;before recharging&quot;, but if I don't put a Fuel, Parts or Mantenaince Drawback, it don't need to be &quot;recharged&quot; no?<br /> <br /> I'm really excited for how you expand on others splats using this! Occultist using Essence as fuel is somewhat one of the pillars of my next Chronicle and having rules to the players imitate them is always useful!</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks! As for your questions:<br /> <br /> * The cloning machine counts as an Active Wonder, and it needs Advanced Duration [+Indefinite Status] so the clones last indefinitely. It also needs Advanced Scale [Subjects] which determines how many clones it can produce per activation. And this would be just Life 5 (Making), plus Conjunction with Mind 5, as per the Create Life spell. You could use more basic Life Practices if the cloning machine has certain limitations (e.g. it has to actually grow the clones in a synthetic womb over time, rather than manifesting an adult human ex nihilo). Do remember that souls cannot be created, not even with Death 5 [Making].<br /> <br /> * Trust me, [Mystery Keys X 10] Successes is nothing. Consider that a Mage with Mind Arcanum 3 can cast Enhance Skill to get Crafts 10. Not only does that increase dice pool AND the maximum number of rolls, there is an official rule in ChroD Core saying any Exceptional Success on an Extended Action can reduce Target Successes by an additional amount equal to [Skill]. And that is before the various dice tricks you can get via thematically fitting spells, usually Ruling or Perfecting. Let's not forget they can benefit from the Equipment, Merits and Teamwork with Cabalmates.<br /> <br /> * Well, that begs a question. If your cloning machine doesn't include Fuel, Parts or Maintenance as Drawbacks... how does it even work? The Drawbacks have to make sense, even if based on esoteric laws of reality. I'll try to add examples of Wonder Invention to the document later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-27T12:45:27-07:00","id":1495673,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... as it turns out, I did not find the motivation to add examples of how Wonders are made... can anybody please suggest 1 to 3 types of typical sci-fi gizmos for me to model? Nothing Archmage-tier like true time travel, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-27T13:32:54-07:00","id":1495676,"title":"","content":"1- A universal remote that uses a sensory version of <i>Coaxing the Spirits</i>.<br /> <br /> 2- A danger detector that uses Death 1 and Time 1 to beep whenever registered subjects are in danger or about to do something dangerous, its volume being directly proportional to the degree of the threat.<br /> <br /> 3- A frozen timepiece that sets the owners's age proportional to the clock's position. It simply changes it rather than temporaly summon them. Somehow it keeps ticking regardless, but only while the owner is alive. <br /> <br /> 4- A stylistic replica of the sampo from Finnish mythology, which produces an <i>Endless Bounty</i> of anything placed in its compartments.<br /> <br /> 5- A &quot;magnet&quot; that looks like a chip with High Speech shaped circuitry on it. It that can be attached to any device, transforming it into a <i>Perpetual Motion</i> machine.<br /> <br /> 6- An extremely comfy pillow that gives a bonus to Willpower recovered by a good night's sleep. Kotatsu and sleeping bag versions are very popular as well.<br /> <br /> 7- A pin that disguises the user's clothes. Guardians use it on the inside of their coats to avoid creating a tell.<br /> <br /> Hope you find your motivation for this one again, its a really cool idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-27-2022, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-27T17:55:52-07:00","id":1495704,"title":"","content":"Relatively low-fiction (or whatever the word is for the sci-fi equivalent of \u2018low fantasy\u2019) suggestions:<br /> <br /> A compass that tells you where you need to go (Fate 1 Serendipity).<br /> <br /> A pill to feign death (Death 2 Suppress Life). <br /> <br /> A spray can that reveals magical formulas as they\u2019re formed (Prime 3 Display of Power).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-29T01:56:15-07:00","id":1495810,"title":"","content":"A flying drone whose propulsion relies on &quot;magnetic fields&quot; or &quot;gravitons&quot; or some similar technobabble, rather than moving components.(Forces 5, Levitate)<br /> <br /> Might be pushing the power-level, but a Stargate-style point-to-point wormhole network. (Space 3, Co-Location) <br /> <br /> Full-body analyzer ala tricorders (Life 1, Analyze Life)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-29T11:49:50-07:00","id":1495840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1484762-homebrew-supernal-invention-system?p=1495676#post1495676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- A universal remote that uses a sensory version of <i>Coaxing the Spirits</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Name:</b> Digital Bypass Key<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> A device which resembles an USB drive, and whose plastic exterior is in the shape of a spider-like key. When inserted into a computer and wound 7 times much like a key, the digital-spirit connected to the computer is compelled to deactivate any mundane security measures that prevent the Wonder's user from accessing the features of the computer. Supernatural security measures trigger a Clash Of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Inventor's Arcana:</b> Spirit 3<br /> <br /> <b>Effects:</b> Coaxing The Spirits [Digital Technology], Channel Essence [Digital Resonance]<br /> <br /> <b>Rating:</b> Highest Practice Level [2] + Extra Practices Taken [1] + Extra Reaching [0] + Every 2 Dots Of Extra Factors [7] - Praxes [1] - Fifth Maneuver Of The Hyper-Tech Prodigy Style [3] - Relevant Digital Or Shamanistic Legacy [1] = 5<br /> <br /> <b>Free Reaching:</b> Instant Casting, More Finely-Tuned Coaxing, Piercing (Coaxing The Spirits), Advanced Duration [+Indefinite] (Channel Essence)<br /> <br /> <b>Extra Reaching:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Free Factors:</b> Standard Potency 3, Standard Duration 1, Standard Scale 1 (Coaxing The Spirits), Standard Potency 3, Advanced Duration 1, Standard Scale 1 (Channel Essence)<br /> <br /> <b>Extra Factors:</b> +6 Potency (+3 For Coaxing The Spirits, +3 For Channel Essence), +4 Dice For Clashes Of Wills Via Piercing (Coaxing The Spirits), +4 Duration (Channel Essence)<br /> <br /> <b>Drawbacks:</b> Attention 1 [The Computer's Screen Shows Brief Glimpses Of What Is Beyond The Gauntlet Around It], Fuel 2 [Essence], Maintenance 1 [Computers], Parts 1 [Sophisticated Microchips Blessed By The Manipulation-Influence Of A Rank 2+ Digital Spirit, Once Per Day For A Full Lunar Cycle]<br /> <br /> <b>Development:</b> 5 Keys<br /> <br /> <b>Example Keys:</b> Find Raw Materials [Assistance From Suitable Rank 2+ Digital Spirit, And Sophisticated Microchips], Designing Schematics &amp; Diagrams [Step By Step Electronics &amp; Programming Guide, Written In Spirit Tongue-Based Script], Prototyping &amp; Testing [Hacking Into The Computer Of A Werewolf Of The Iron Masters Tribe]<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Piercing is a house rule. It is a generic +1 Reach Option which, once selected, allows the Mage to apply a -2 to spellcasting in exchange for a +1 to Clashes Of Wills, up to a -8 penalty for a +4 bonus. This does not stack with bonuses for Clashes Of Wills granted by Advanced Duration. Instead, Piercing effectively allows you to improve Clashes Of Wills for spells whose effects don't make sense for Advanced Duration. This is especially useful for combat and healing spells. For this Wonder, 2 extra dots of Spell Factors have been applied to Piercing. Since +1 dot of Spell Factors requires a -2 penalty to the spell version, then the Wonder has 2 X 2 = 4 bonus dice for Clashes Of Wills involving Coaxing The Spirits.<br /> <br /> The Channel Essence spell has been included in order to give onboard storage of up to 6 Essence for the activation of the Wonder. If the user wants, he can coax the digital-spirit into reestablishing the security measures once the user is done hacking, creating decoy files, changing dates of access, and other auxiliary tactics to make it seem as if the computer was never hacked. However, this still does not allow the digital-spirit to do anything that would require an Extended Action, and a dedicated and perceptive IT professional may still notice something is amiss since the Wonder does not include any Veiling effects. Supernatural means of detecting that the computer has been tampered with will work normally. This Wonder has a small spider-like tell in its exterior design to make the Rank 2+ Digital Spirit feel happy, because he looks like a spider made of 1s and 0s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-29-2022, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-30T14:37:29-07:00","id":1495909,"title":"","content":"This is awesome - great work!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/494367/The-Lost-Athanaeum?affiliate_id=1564482\" target=\"_blank\">The Lost Athanaeum</a> Mage adventure is now live on Storyteller's Vault!<br /> If you want to see it in play, check out <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500596-dimensions-unseen-mage-2e-actual-play-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">Dimensions Unseen</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27424-phoog","name":"Phoog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T19:42:40-08:00","id":1503789,"title":"","content":"Added several examples of Wonders to the GoogleDoc linked in the original post. Do tell me what y'all think, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"ht